WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.156
When Rosa applies, the insurer may order an investigative

00:00:03.156 --> 00:00:05.962
consumer report about her character, reputation and lifestyle.

00:00:05.962 --> 00:00:09.819
The Fair Credit Reporting Act requires that she be told, within

00:00:09.819 --> 00:00:13.677
three days of the request, that such a report may be

00:00:13.677 --> 00:00:17.535
made, and that she may ask about its nature and scope.

00:00:17.535 --> 00:00:21.743
If the insurer takes adverse action based on a report, such as

00:00:21.743 --> 00:00:25.951
declining or rating her, it must tell her and identify the reporting

00:00:25.951 --> 00:00:29.458
agency so she can obtain the report and dispute errors.

00:00:29.458 --> 00:00:32.614
Producers who collect applications must know these notices exist

00:00:32.614 --> 00:00:35.420
and never discourage an applicant from exercising them.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:41.069
Federal law treats insurance fraud affecting interstate commerce as a crime.

00:00:41.069 --> 00:00:46.718
Under 18 USC 1033, anyone convicted of a felony involving dishonesty

00:00:46.718 --> 00:00:52.366
or breach of trust may not work in the business of

00:00:52.366 --> 00:00:57.502
insurance without the written consent of the state insurance regulator.

00:00:57.502 --> 00:01:02.637
The same statute punishes false statements to regulators, embezzlement of

00:01:02.637 --> 00:01:07.772
insurer funds and threats against regulators or examiners, with prison

00:01:07.772 --> 00:01:12.908
terms that grow when the conduct jeopardizes an insurer’s safety.

00:01:12.908 --> 00:01:18.556
Section 1034 lets the Attorney General seek civil penalties and injunctions.

00:01:18.556 --> 00:01:23.178
For Theo the practical rule is simple: a disqualifying

00:01:23.178 --> 00:01:27.800
conviction requires a consent letter before any insurance work.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:31.499
The Employee Retirement Income Security Act governs employee benefit plans

00:01:31.499 --> 00:01:35.198
sponsored by private employers, including group health and disability plans.

00:01:35.198 --> 00:01:37.787
Government and church plans are generally exempt.

00:01:37.787 --> 00:01:41.486
Anyone who controls plan assets or administration is a fiduciary

00:01:41.486 --> 00:01:45.185
and must act solely in the interest of participants, with

00:01:45.185 --> 00:01:48.884
the care of a prudent person, following the plan documents.

00:01:48.884 --> 00:01:53.323
Plans must report to the Department of Labor, usually on Form 5500,

00:01:53.323 --> 00:01:57.762
and must disclose terms to participants through a summary plan description delivered

00:01:57.762 --> 00:02:01.461
within 90 days of joining, plus summaries of material changes.

00:02:01.461 --> 00:02:05.900
When Priya offers a group plan, ERISA shapes her duties as sponsor.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:10.108
COBRA applies to employers with 20 or more employees

00:02:10.108 --> 00:02:14.316
on a typical business day in the prior year.

00:02:14.316 --> 00:02:19.459
A worker who loses coverage through termination, other than gross misconduct,

00:02:19.459 --> 00:02:24.602
or reduced hours may continue the group plan for 18 months,

00:02:24.602 --> 00:02:29.745
extended to 29 months if disabled within the first 60 days.

00:02:29.745 --> 00:02:33.485
Death of the employee, divorce, Medicare entitlement or

00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:37.226
a child aging out gives dependents 36 months.

00:02:37.226 --> 00:02:43.304
The employer notifies the plan administrator within 30 days, the administrator notifies the

00:02:43.304 --> 00:02:48.915
beneficiary within 14 days, and the beneficiary has 60 days to elect.

00:02:48.915 --> 00:02:53.590
The premium may reach 102 percent of the group cost.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:56.875
The ACA rewrote the rules for comprehensive medical coverage.

00:02:56.875 --> 00:03:00.161
Individual health insurance coverage means coverage sold to individuals

00:03:00.161 --> 00:03:03.446
in the individual market, as opposed to group plans.

00:03:03.446 --> 00:03:07.462
Plans must cover children on a parent’s policy to age 26.

00:03:07.462 --> 00:03:12.208
They may not impose lifetime dollar limits, or annual dollar limits, on essential

00:03:12.208 --> 00:03:16.953
health benefits, the ten categories every individual and small group plan must include.

00:03:16.953 --> 00:03:21.334
Premiums may vary only by age, within a 3 to 1 ratio,

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:25.714
tobacco use up to 1.5 to 1, geographic area and family size.

00:03:25.714 --> 00:03:29.730
Group plans may not impose waiting periods longer than 90 days.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:34.924
The National Association of Insurance Commissioners is the organization of the chief

00:03:34.924 --> 00:03:40.119
insurance regulators of the states, the District of Columbia and the territories.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:45.746
It drafts model laws and regulations, such as the uniform health policy provisions

00:03:45.746 --> 00:03:50.940
you will study in Lesson 15, and it accredits state insurance departments.

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:55.269
The NAIC is not a federal agency and has no

00:03:55.269 --> 00:03:59.164
power to license producers, approve policies or enforce anything.

00:03:59.164 --> 00:04:03.060
A model becomes law in Maryland only when the

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:06.523
General Assembly or the Insurance Commissioner adopts it.

00:04:06.523 --> 00:04:12.150
When a producer says the NAIC approved a policy, that statement is false.
